@title Release board: plan, tune and sort
# Release board

Sort the tickets, tune eight rollout settings, switch three flags, and copy the changes back to the agent. This page is the large
case for the shell: thirty items to place, eight numbers, three switches and a long runbook that fills as you edit.

ask owner | Who signs off on this release?

param canary unit=% | Canary share | 5 0 100 5
param ramp unit=%/day | Ramp per day | 10 0 50 1
param timeout unit=ms | Request timeout | 800 100 5000 50
param retries | Retries before giving up | 2 0 10 1
param burst unit=req/s | Burst allowance | 120 0 1000 10
param cache unit=min | Cache lifetime | 15 1 240 1
param soak unit=h | Soak time before the next step | 6 0 48 2
param budget unit=% | Error budget left to hold | 2.5 0 10 0.5

toggle checkout_v2 on | Serve the new checkout
toggle express needs=checkout_v2 | Express checkout
toggle saved_cards on needs=checkout_v2,express | Saved cards on the express path

bucket triage | Now, Next, Later, Cut | Where does each ticket go?
triage: ENG-2041 Fix duplicate receipt emails | Now
triage: ENG-2047 Rotate the signing secret | Now
triage: "ENG-2052 Retry, then give up" | Next
triage: ENG-2058 Cache the price table | Next
triage: ENG-2063 Drop the legacy cookie | Later
triage: "ENG-2066 Align the ""Pay"" button label" | Next
triage: ENG-2071 Backfill order totals | Now
triage: ENG-2074 Rename the queue: orders-v2 | Later
triage: ENG-2079 Add a health probe | Now
triage: "ENG-2083 Trim logging; keep the audit trail" | Next
triage: ENG-2086 Upgrade the card form | Later
triage: ENG-2090 Remove the unused flag | Cut
triage: ENG-2092 Replace moment.js with date-fns | Next
triage: ENG-2095 Document the rollback | Now
triage: ENG-2098 Throttle the export job | Later
triage: ENG-2101 Fix the 404 on the receipt page | Now
triage: ENG-2104 Split the monolith | Cut
triage: ENG-2107 Add dark mode to the receipt | Later
triage: ENG-2110 Rate-limit the lookup | Next
triage: ENG-2113 Migrate the cron jobs | Later
triage: ENG-2116 Stop retrying on 4xx | Now
triage: ENG-2119 Pin the base image | Next
triage: ENG-2122 Review the CSP report | Now
triage: ENG-2125 Remove the beta banner | Cut
triage: ENG-2128 Index the orders table | Next
triage: ENG-2131 Speed up the cart page | Later
triage: ENG-2134 Fix the tax rounding | Now
triage: ENG-2137 Switch the mailer | Later
triage: ENG-2140 Archive old sessions | Cut
triage: ENG-2143 Add the on-call runbook link | Next

template runbook | Runbook for the on-call engineer
```text
Release runbook. Owner: {owner}.

1. Send {canary} of traffic to the new build and watch the error rate for {soak}.
2. If the error budget left is above {budget}, raise the share by {ramp} per day; otherwise hold and page the owner.
3. Every request times out after {timeout} and is retried {retries} times with a short pause between tries.
4. Allow bursts of {burst} and keep cached prices for {cache}; never cache a signed-in basket.
5. The new checkout is {checkout_v2}. Express checkout is {express}. Saved cards on the express path are {saved_cards}.

Rollback: switch the new checkout off, wait for the queue to drain, then confirm the old path takes orders.
Do not edit the flags by hand while a step is soaking; ask {owner} first and write the reason in the channel.
Escalate to the owner after two failed steps, and to the platform team after three. Keep this page open until the
last ticket is closed, and paste the final export into the release notes so the next shift starts from the same numbers.

Checks before each step: the dashboards load, the synthetic order completes in under {timeout}, and the retry count on the
payment provider has not moved. Checks after each step: the queue depth is flat, the cache hit rate is steady with a
lifetime of {cache}, and no ticket from the Now column has been reopened. {owner} signs the final step.
Contacts: the platform team keeps a rota in the usual place; the payments provider has a status page and a phone line.
If the provider is down, do not retry beyond {retries} tries; hold the step and tell {owner}.
```

